WEBVTT

00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:21.390
This can't be happening; I clasp my head in my hands

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:27.980
As I struggle with my desire to escape from this saturated world.

00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:33.400
Time goes flowing past with the rustling roar of sand.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:36.820
Things never get any better.

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:39.740
I'm gazing on toward a dreamless tomorrow.

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:47.040
I want to bid farewell to my days of constantly feeling lost.

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:52.510
I try stretching out my hand in resistance.

00:00:52.510 --> 00:00:58.260
We'll cry millions upon millions of tears, then be reborn.

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:04.390
Let's keep going, with red in our eyes, toward the future we drew for ourselves.

00:01:04.390 --> 00:01:10.150
Come over to me; I'm clapping my hands.

00:01:10.150 --> 00:01:12.110
Who are you? Where are you coming from?

00:01:12.110 --> 00:01:16.450
I strain my eyes in the darkness.

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:22.030
I can't see a thing, and nothing makes sense, but I'll go anyway.

00:01:22.030 --> 00:01:28.540
To the place where you're waiting, lit by a beacon of light.

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:34.680
Ah, what should I do?

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:37.090
All of the world,

00:01:37.090 --> 00:01:40.360
is reflected so beautifully.

00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:45.100
Just that fact is enough, isn't it?

00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:45.100
Whoa, this is amazing!

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:48.530
Dol-pli, huh?

00:01:48.530 --> 00:01:50.060
Drill pudding?

00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:51.920
It's called an idol application.

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:53.900
A computerised dress-up doll.

00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:55.730
We're sure making progress in a lot of ways lately.

00:01:55.730 --> 00:01:57.900
You're lining up even though you didn't know?

00:01:57.900 --> 00:01:59.460
I'm doing a job.

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:01.940
I was asked to go buy the new...

00:02:01.940 --> 00:02:03.750
...what was it?

00:02:03.750 --> 00:02:05.070
A song.

00:02:05.070 --> 00:02:09.870
A song!

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:09.370
A song, right?

00:02:09.870 --> 00:02:12.530
The new song release and voice data.

00:02:12.530 --> 00:02:14.890
It's completely different than that old Vocaloid thing.

00:02:14.890 --> 00:02:17.750
It's 100% indistinguishable from a real person!

00:02:17.750 --> 00:02:20.260
I've only heard a sample, but it sure was awesome.

00:02:20.260 --> 00:02:22.030
Yeah, the song was great, too!

00:02:22.030 --> 00:02:23.470
It kinda reminded me of "Yonaga".

00:02:23.470 --> 00:02:25.160
He shouldn't have said that.

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:26.510
Yeah, Yonaga's a bit taboo around here.

00:02:26.510 --> 00:02:27.780
Geez...

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:29.160
That's dangerous to say.

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:34.230
The only songs that go up on the net are
ones that have been thoroughly checked.

00:02:36.870 --> 00:02:38.520
Excuse me!

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:43.850
The Dol-pli expansion data that was supposed to go on sale today has been banned.

00:02:45.910 --> 00:02:47.240
What the hell are you saying?!

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:48.840
You have to be joking!

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:50.710
How long do you think we've been waiting in line?

00:02:50.710 --> 00:02:52.500
It's not like you're running a food stand!

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:54.340
What do you mean, "banned"?

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:55.210
It was probably cancelled!

00:02:55.830 --> 00:02:57.240
Shut up already!

00:02:57.240 --> 00:02:58.780
I'm troubled by this, too!

00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:00.110
Coming through.

00:03:04.590 --> 00:03:05.850
Oh, this is terrible!

00:03:05.850 --> 00:03:06.680
What's wrong?

00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:10.500
A woman, who had boarded a white, unlicensed taxi,

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:13.940
told the driver she had forgotten an important piece of luggage.

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:16.600
I have somewhere else I need to be.

00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:20.700
Driver, would you pick up and deliver my luggage for me?

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:22.170
Please.

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:27.420
Just as he was told, the driver went to retrieve
the luggage from the place he'd been directed.

00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:29.390
Which was the mansion of Osada Hisako,

00:03:29.390 --> 00:03:31.690
a Yokohama investor, correct?

00:03:31.690 --> 00:03:36.650
When he arrived at the Osada residence there was a suitcase being held by the gatekeeper, just as the woman had said.

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:43.510
Realising that it may hold something valuable, he opened it,

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:49.350
but inside was the mansion's owner, Osada Hisako herself.

00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:51.080
Interesting.

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:54.910
Koyama-san, my father is merely in the business of supplying information.

00:03:54.910 --> 00:03:56.570
He isn't a detective.

00:03:56.570 --> 00:03:57.740
Don't worry about it.

00:03:57.740 --> 00:03:59.820
This has piqued my interest.

00:03:59.820 --> 00:04:03.680
I have no choice but to depend on the chairman, as this case has many mysteries surrounding it.

00:04:05.030 --> 00:04:08.280
The culprit isn't the woman who hired the unlicensed taxi?

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:11.290
The suitcase had been left there by a different person: a man!

00:04:12.740 --> 00:04:17.420
He left a memo saying "A white taxi will come to pick it up, so please hold onto it until then"!

00:04:18.210 --> 00:04:20.510
The gatekeeper tried to refuse, but...

00:04:22.540 --> 00:04:26.550
We believe that Osada Hisako was
murdered while she was out on business.

00:04:26.550 --> 00:04:32.750
Why did the culprit go through the trouble of putting the corpse in a suitcase and leaving it at the victim's mansion then?

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:36.610
And what's his relation to the white taxi woman?

00:04:36.610 --> 00:04:39.060
Well, the truth of that very matter is...

00:04:40.070 --> 00:04:44.450
The suspect is restaurant proprietor Aramaki Toshiji, 47 years old.

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:50.820
He became the lover of Osada Hisako in the years following the death of her husband.

00:04:50.820 --> 00:04:54.960
I've heard that Aramaki has quite the strange hobby.

00:05:00.670 --> 00:05:03.500
Aramaki cross-dresses as a hobby.

00:05:03.500 --> 00:05:06.830
That means that the man who left behind the suitcase...

00:05:06.830 --> 00:05:10.390
...and the woman in the white taxi were both Aramaki in disguise.

00:05:10.890 --> 00:05:17.100
Aramaki was trying to remove himself from suspicion by
creating the expectation of two criminals working together.

00:05:17.100 --> 00:05:21.400
At the moment, we are putting all of our efforts into finding Aramaki.

00:05:23.740 --> 00:05:25.600
It's so beautiful,

00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:32.660
Yokohama... Blue Light Yokohama...

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:37.630
No matter how far we walk,

00:05:37.630 --> 00:05:42.000
it's like being in a tiny boat.

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:44.880
I-

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:50.430
You have such a beautiful voice. I couldn't help myself!

00:05:52.310 --> 00:05:55.310
Thank you. You're the detective, right?

00:05:56.810 --> 00:06:00.380
You want to find the person that killed your mum?

00:06:00.380 --> 00:06:03.940
If that's the case, didn't Kaishou Rinroku reach a conclusion a few days ago?

00:06:04.690 --> 00:06:06.690
Uncle Aramaki isn't the murderer!

00:06:07.370 --> 00:06:08.950
He's hiding, isn't he?

00:06:11.470 --> 00:06:15.430
My mother had been receiving threats for a long time.

00:06:16.160 --> 00:06:19.330
Every month she would deliver money to a hotel in Shinagawa.

00:06:19.830 --> 00:06:20.540
Shinagawa?

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:24.090
Please deliver the suitcase to the Toukyuu Hotel in Shinagawa.

00:06:24.630 --> 00:06:27.140
That sounds fishy, Shinjuurou.

00:06:27.140 --> 00:06:29.220
So, the person that was threatening her...?

00:06:31.380 --> 00:06:33.100
Possibly someone from Yonagahime...

00:06:35.290 --> 00:06:37.170
No, I have no idea!

00:06:37.170 --> 00:06:40.100
But the culprit must be someone else.

00:06:41.380 --> 00:06:48.400
Understood! Please leave everything to this Defeated Detective, Yuuki Shinjuurou!

00:06:51.880 --> 00:06:56.370
The lights of the city are so beautiful, aren't they?

00:06:56.370 --> 00:06:58.500
Yokohama...

00:06:57.020 --> 00:06:58.500
Ah, that's the song from before!

00:07:00.370 --> 00:07:02.630
My grandmother taught it to me.

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:04.560
Ah.

00:07:04.560 --> 00:07:09.760
In my grandmother's country, it was illegal to
play Japanese songs on the radio or television.

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:16.110
Nonetheless, this song became popular and everyone would sing it secretly.

00:07:16.110 --> 00:07:18.520
The power of music is incredible, isn't it?

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:21.390
Are you perchance aiming to be a singer?

00:07:23.510 --> 00:07:27.600
Yes. At one point, I thought it might be impossible,

00:07:27.600 --> 00:07:30.280
but I've realised that I mustn't give up on my dream.

00:07:31.400 --> 00:07:34.410
Because you believe that it will eventually come true?

00:07:43.350 --> 00:07:44.960
What's wrong, Shinjuurou?

00:07:45.780 --> 00:07:47.940
Even if the culprit was Aramaki,

00:07:47.940 --> 00:07:52.240
why would he leave the suitcase at the victim's home?

00:07:52.240 --> 00:07:53.590
What are you trying to say?

00:07:54.580 --> 00:07:57.720
Yonagahime... Yonaga...

00:08:03.450 --> 00:08:06.110
All images and sounds of Yonagahime have been removed from the net.

00:08:06.570 --> 00:08:10.860
If anyone re-uploads them, they'll be arrested
under the New Information Privacy Protection Act.

00:08:11.340 --> 00:08:13.860
Do you seriously not know anything about Yonagahime?

00:08:14.640 --> 00:08:16.370
Well, I wasn't in Japan at the time.

00:08:21.530 --> 00:08:23.500
This is a version of it programmed through Dol-pli.

00:08:37.390 --> 00:08:38.930
Whoa.

00:08:40.790 --> 00:08:43.580
The world comes awake,

00:08:43.580 --> 00:08:46.600
as the dawn nears.

00:08:46.890 --> 00:08:50.360
Shining beautifully,

00:08:51.560 --> 00:08:54.330
until the end.

00:08:56.580 --> 00:08:58.570
They became national idols.

00:08:59.350 --> 00:09:02.700
During the war, there wasn't a single day that they didn't appear on TV.

00:09:03.140 --> 00:09:05.100
"Let's strike back against terrorist attacks!"

00:09:05.100 --> 00:09:06.820
"Let's send out a massive amount of troops!"

00:09:06.820 --> 00:09:09.030
The lyrics were strongly influencing public opinion,

00:09:09.030 --> 00:09:12.670
so the Public Prosecutor's office prohibited it from being broadcast.

00:09:13.100 --> 00:09:14.720
What's the "3+1" mean?

00:09:14.720 --> 00:09:20.220
"Yonagahime 3+1". There's actually a whole story behind it.

00:09:28.600 --> 00:09:29.980
What is this?

00:09:30.580 --> 00:09:33.610
Yonagahime was originally supposed to be a four person group, apparently.

00:09:33.610 --> 00:09:39.540
But just before their début, one of the members became a victim of the very first terrorist attack on Tokyo.

00:09:39.540 --> 00:09:41.740
It's known as the "12/23 Attack".

00:09:42.130 --> 00:09:46.210
Her image was even captured on surveillance cameras.

00:09:48.640 --> 00:09:50.430
Eri isn't dead!

00:09:50.430 --> 00:09:52.730
She's here with us!

00:09:52.730 --> 00:09:55.250
The four of us together are Yonagahime.

00:09:56.010 --> 00:10:00.050
We'll never lose, never cry!

00:10:00.050 --> 00:10:01.760
We're going to take back our dream!

00:10:01.760 --> 00:10:03.760
Please, listen!

00:10:04.120 --> 00:10:08.100
It was this moment that sent their popularity sky-high.

00:10:08.100 --> 00:10:12.270
They even used Eri's voice, which had been pre-recorded.

00:10:12.270 --> 00:10:14.270
Rise up, (You...)

00:10:14.270 --> 00:10:16.320
it's time, (...already know.)

00:10:16.320 --> 00:10:18.660
to depart.

00:10:18.660 --> 00:10:21.570
Though our wings are broken from the fall...

00:10:22.090 --> 00:10:25.880
Forever we will,

00:10:22.650 --> 00:10:26.370
That's rumoured to be Eri's voice.

00:10:25.880 --> 00:10:29.830
bathe in sorrow,

00:10:29.830 --> 00:10:33.830
We will protect praying maidens everywhere...

00:10:38.870 --> 00:10:41.560
Even after my little sister dissolved Yonagahime,

00:10:41.560 --> 00:10:43.140
she wanted to continue solo.

00:10:43.720 --> 00:10:45.880
But Osada-san was against it.

00:10:45.880 --> 00:10:48.090
Osada? Do you mean Osada Hisako-san?

00:10:48.090 --> 00:10:49.210
Yeah.

00:10:54.610 --> 00:10:57.280
What connection did Osada Hisako-san have with Yonagahime?

00:10:57.570 --> 00:11:00.950
She was the president of the agency. The group's founder.

00:11:05.580 --> 00:11:10.060
...our words of love, Yokohama...

00:11:09.270 --> 00:11:10.580
Shinjuurou!

00:11:10.060 --> 00:11:14.880
...Blue Light Yokohama.

00:11:10.580 --> 00:11:12.670
They're both already here!

00:11:12.670 --> 00:11:14.640
Yonaga! Yonaga!

00:11:14.640 --> 00:11:15.740
You idiot!

00:11:21.340 --> 00:11:23.410
Yumeno-san and Kumi-san, correct?

00:11:23.410 --> 00:11:24.640
Yonaga! Yonaga!

00:11:24.960 --> 00:11:26.630
P-Please stop that!

00:11:26.630 --> 00:11:29.770
The authorities know who killed Osada-san, don't they?

00:11:30.430 --> 00:11:34.500
I hear the two of you were coming to meet the victim here once a month.

00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:35.430
That's-

00:11:35.430 --> 00:11:36.800
I looked into it.

00:11:36.800 --> 00:11:38.760
The victim was being threatened by someone.

00:11:38.760 --> 00:11:41.240
That's not... the president was just...

00:11:41.240 --> 00:11:43.530
Osada-san was worried about us,

00:11:43.530 --> 00:11:44.990
so she tried to cover our living expenses.

00:11:44.990 --> 00:11:48.660
Lady, when you're not talking, you could be mistaken for a man.

00:11:49.640 --> 00:11:53.870
The people who handled Osada Hisako's body
were said to be a mysterious man and woman.

00:11:53.870 --> 00:11:55.190
You must be joking!

00:11:55.190 --> 00:11:57.530
Are you saying that we had a hand in the president's death?!

00:11:57.530 --> 00:11:58.630
I'm wrong?

00:11:59.060 --> 00:12:01.590
Yes, of course you are!

00:12:01.590 --> 00:12:05.470
Now that the president is gone, I have no idea how I'll live my life.

00:12:09.740 --> 00:12:11.910
At first glance, a male and female duo.

00:12:11.910 --> 00:12:13.240
A Shinagawa hotel.

00:12:13.240 --> 00:12:14.850
A closely entangled relationship with Osada Hisako.

00:12:16.030 --> 00:12:19.150
It seems that someone wanted us to think you two were the culprits.

00:12:20.070 --> 00:12:20.900
Someone?

00:12:23.260 --> 00:12:26.030
What if it's Eri-chan's ghost?!

00:12:27.700 --> 00:12:30.240
Eri died... in the "12/23 Attack".

00:12:33.090 --> 00:12:33.750
Yumeno?!

00:12:37.460 --> 00:12:38.090
Inga!

00:12:40.770 --> 00:12:44.300
I can't... I can't hold it in any longer, Shinjuurou!

00:12:46.150 --> 00:12:47.010
What's wrong?

00:12:47.010 --> 00:12:48.550
What are you playing dumb for?

00:12:48.950 --> 00:12:50.700
You know well enough...

00:12:50.700 --> 00:12:52.640
...where the truth lies.

00:12:52.640 --> 00:12:55.140
But we don't know the motive.

00:12:55.620 --> 00:12:57.650
Let's just clear that up, then.

00:13:03.710 --> 00:13:05.690
You said it yourself,

00:13:05.690 --> 00:13:08.990
"I'll show you what a real human is."

00:13:08.990 --> 00:13:11.540
"I'll show you the truth about humans."

00:13:12.020 --> 00:13:16.040
I know, but I still don't know the truth...

00:13:16.040 --> 00:13:17.420
You're lying!

00:13:18.360 --> 00:13:20.070
What are you seeking?

00:13:20.070 --> 00:13:22.370
What are you trying to protect?

00:13:22.370 --> 00:13:24.170
Oh, kind Shinjuurou...

00:13:24.850 --> 00:13:26.930
Is the one you feel sorry for that girl?

00:13:27.300 --> 00:13:28.600
Yourself?

00:13:29.190 --> 00:13:32.930
Even if you pity yourself, nothing will change.

00:13:32.930 --> 00:13:35.560
Tell me. What should I ask?

00:13:45.940 --> 00:13:47.950
Come, answer me.

00:13:48.460 --> 00:13:51.700
Who is the real fourth member of Yonagahime?

00:13:51.700 --> 00:13:55.330
I'm not supposed to tell anyone.

00:13:58.820 --> 00:14:00.230
Don't bother resisting.

00:14:00.230 --> 00:14:02.830
People have no choice but to answer her question.

00:14:03.450 --> 00:14:04.840
Her one, single question.

00:14:05.190 --> 00:14:06.340
Answer me!

00:14:07.100 --> 00:14:09.590
Who is the fourth member of Yonagahime?

00:14:11.090 --> 00:14:12.490
Who?!

00:14:17.380 --> 00:14:19.350
Yonagahime was a three person group.

00:14:24.370 --> 00:14:27.190
What about Anzai Eri, who was caught up in the terrorist attack?

00:14:27.740 --> 00:14:29.440
When our début was decided upon,

00:14:29.440 --> 00:14:31.870
Osada-san brought that video with her.

00:14:32.490 --> 00:14:37.120
She said we'd pretend that the girl was one of us.

00:14:37.120 --> 00:14:39.990
They even had a track of her singing.

00:14:39.990 --> 00:14:43.250
We'd never even met a girl named Eri!

00:14:44.150 --> 00:14:45.930
But we couldn't refuse;

00:14:45.930 --> 00:14:48.550
they said we'd become stars!

00:14:49.550 --> 00:14:52.710
When the war ended, Yonagahime was dissolved.

00:14:53.370 --> 00:14:55.760
We were warned never to tell the truth about "Eri".

00:14:56.140 --> 00:14:57.850
That if we did...

00:14:58.770 --> 00:15:03.350
The lights of the city are so beautiful...

00:15:04.270 --> 00:15:06.830
A-Are you sure about this?

00:15:07.650 --> 00:15:12.660
No matter how far we walk...

00:15:21.620 --> 00:15:22.640
Hello?

00:15:23.480 --> 00:15:24.210
Yes...

00:15:24.210 --> 00:15:26.250
Why? What are you saying?!

00:15:26.250 --> 00:15:27.970
Why did it get cancelled?!

00:15:31.690 --> 00:15:34.260
It's hopeless... there's really bad reception out here.

00:15:34.260 --> 00:15:35.730
I lost the call.

00:15:35.730 --> 00:15:37.570
There were two culprits.

00:15:37.570 --> 00:15:40.140
They were receiving money from your mother each month,

00:15:40.510 --> 00:15:43.380
and meeting in a Shinagawa hotel.

00:15:43.380 --> 00:15:47.520
The only people that fit that description are Yumeno-san and Kumi-san of Yonagahime.

00:15:49.040 --> 00:15:51.820
I... I can't believe those two would...

00:15:51.820 --> 00:15:54.160
But... I see, if Kumi-san disguised herself,

00:15:54.160 --> 00:15:56.950
she could appear to be a man...

00:15:59.300 --> 00:16:01.670
...which is what you wanted everyone to think.

00:16:01.670 --> 00:16:05.020
But Kaishou ended up selecting someone else as the murderer.

00:16:05.020 --> 00:16:05.710
Did you panic?

00:16:06.680 --> 00:16:08.340
What are you... talking about?

00:16:09.240 --> 00:16:11.590
Anzai Eri, who's supposedly resting here...

00:16:11.990 --> 00:16:14.470
...that's you, isn't it? Osada An-san.

00:16:15.910 --> 00:16:19.470
When Osada Hisako brought about the début of Yonagahime,

00:16:19.470 --> 00:16:23.410
she created a fictional member that was killed in a terrorist attack,

00:16:23.410 --> 00:16:26.650
and used your exceptional voice to corroborate the story.

00:16:28.210 --> 00:16:30.000
I analysed it.

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:33.030
Your voice matches "Anzai Eri's" almost perfectly.

00:16:33.030 --> 00:16:37.950
It's also nearly identical to the Dol-pli expansion
data that was taken off the market the other day.

00:16:38.690 --> 00:16:40.350
Is that so?

00:16:40.350 --> 00:16:41.700
I had my doubts from the beginning.

00:16:42.970 --> 00:16:47.210
Why would the culprit go through all the trouble of delivering the suitcase to the victim's home?

00:16:47.750 --> 00:16:53.460
It was so that anyone who lived there wouldn't be considered as a suspect. Isn't that so, Osada An?

00:16:56.950 --> 00:16:59.460
I wanted to sing.

00:16:59.460 --> 00:17:00.780
I'm sure you did.

00:17:00.780 --> 00:17:03.410
Your singing is wonderful.

00:17:05.740 --> 00:17:08.310
I was a child when Yonagahime was formed,

00:17:08.310 --> 00:17:10.590
so I didn't understand any of it then.

00:17:10.590 --> 00:17:14.680
I wasn't bothered by my voice being used for "Anzai Eri".

00:17:14.680 --> 00:17:17.990
After all, I was able to hear my voice on TV every single day.

00:17:18.880 --> 00:17:20.800
But then the war ended...

00:17:20.800 --> 00:17:23.990
And Japan, having lost the war, was so depressed...

00:17:23.990 --> 00:17:26.750
...I felt that I had to cheer everyone up with my singing.

00:17:27.370 --> 00:17:29.940
But Mum told me I couldn't sing!

00:17:29.940 --> 00:17:33.500
And all of my offers began to fall through.

00:17:33.500 --> 00:17:35.260
I didn't want to give up!

00:17:35.800 --> 00:17:38.130
I wanted to believe that my dream would come true!

00:17:39.590 --> 00:17:43.720
That's why I thought Dol-pli data would be the
perfect solution, since my name wouldn't be on it,

00:17:44.000 --> 00:17:46.030
but she said I couldn't do that either.

00:17:46.030 --> 00:17:50.480
She said there were people who would be troubled, should anyone recognise the voice of a dead girl.

00:17:50.480 --> 00:17:54.990
They were stolen from me... my songs... Yonagahime...

00:17:54.990 --> 00:17:56.490
...all because of my mother!

00:17:57.500 --> 00:18:04.620
Forever we will bathe in sorrow,

00:18:05.210 --> 00:18:12.500
we will protect praying maidens everywhere.

00:18:12.500 --> 00:18:16.590
The tears that appear in their eyes,

00:18:16.590 --> 00:18:20.480
are from committing the greatest sin.

00:18:20.480 --> 00:18:28.030
Wave your flag of courage lovingly...

00:18:30.930 --> 00:18:36.250
And still... in that last phone call I was turned down for a singing career.

00:18:36.250 --> 00:18:39.030
The suspect, Aramaki, was found as a corpse.

00:18:39.710 --> 00:18:41.350
It was a crime of passion.

00:18:41.350 --> 00:18:43.700
He committed suicide as soon as he realised he couldn't escape.

00:18:44.060 --> 00:18:45.060
You killed him?

00:18:45.060 --> 00:18:46.450
Kaishou's deduction, huh?

00:18:47.580 --> 00:18:49.530
The murderer was Aramaki.

00:18:49.530 --> 00:18:53.330
Nonetheless, Osada An's voice will not be made public.

00:18:54.370 --> 00:18:57.490
This measure is in compliance with the
New Information Privacy Protection Act.

00:18:57.490 --> 00:18:59.270
No...

00:18:59.270 --> 00:19:03.720
Then... for what reason did I kill my Mum?

00:19:04.890 --> 00:19:07.000
Oh? Is she having a breakdown?

00:19:07.000 --> 00:19:08.470
Of course she is.

00:19:09.290 --> 00:19:12.460
People die. Things break down.

00:19:12.460 --> 00:19:13.980
Nothing is unbreakable.

00:19:14.940 --> 00:19:17.210
So being, I will break as well.

00:19:17.210 --> 00:19:19.080
I'm merely searching.

00:19:19.080 --> 00:19:20.970
Why search?

00:19:20.970 --> 00:19:23.930
Because I'm not important enough to afford living without searching.

00:19:23.930 --> 00:19:25.830
I will keep searching.

00:19:25.830 --> 00:19:27.120
Kaishou Rinroku!

00:19:27.540 --> 00:19:32.480
You were the ones that created the story that
Anzai Eri was a victim of terrorism, weren't you?

00:19:32.480 --> 00:19:34.000
The images of Eri were fake as well.

00:19:35.240 --> 00:19:38.570
Yonagahime was an idol group formed for the purpose of raising wartime spirits.

00:19:38.570 --> 00:19:41.790
But after the war, you knew there'd be trouble if anyone found out.

00:19:41.790 --> 00:19:43.260
That's why you people...

00:19:43.670 --> 00:19:46.360
How terrible! A conspiracy theory?

00:19:48.130 --> 00:19:50.930
All right! Let's get started!

00:20:21.780 --> 00:20:23.300
Damn!

00:20:22.130 --> 00:20:23.300
What the hell, man?

00:20:23.300 --> 00:20:27.350
The lights of the city are so beautiful, aren't they?

00:20:27.350 --> 00:20:29.390
Yokohama...

00:20:29.760 --> 00:20:35.980
Blue Light Yokohama... with you.

00:20:36.450 --> 00:20:39.380
In respect to the recent murder of a young woman, the conclusion...

00:20:39.380 --> 00:20:43.150
...reached by Kaishou Rinroku of JJ Networking has been verified.

00:20:41.690 --> 00:20:43.150
Mr. Detective?

00:20:43.150 --> 00:20:48.700
As always, our words of love, Yokohama...

00:20:58.210 --> 00:21:02.680
No matter how far we walk,

00:21:02.680 --> 00:21:06.910
it's like being in a tiny boat.

00:21:06.910 --> 00:21:20.170
I rock... rock within your arms.

00:21:29.370 --> 00:21:37.420
Wandering hazily on a pale morning, hearing a whispered prayer,

00:21:37.420 --> 00:21:45.380
You and I trace a twisted scenery.

00:21:45.380 --> 00:21:53.060
We're seeking the (truth). "We don't even care if it's a lie."

00:21:53.520 --> 00:21:57.440
As if we can see right through it,

00:21:59.520 --> 00:22:01.400
We follow it along.

00:22:01.400 --> 00:22:05.360
Looking for, going beyond words,

00:22:05.440 --> 00:22:09.360
Like a falling feather.

00:22:09.360 --> 00:22:12.490
Looking for, find it,

00:22:13.370 --> 00:22:18.830
So we can come closer together.

00:22:33.350 --> 00:22:37.350
Looking for, unravel it,

00:22:37.350 --> 00:22:41.350
Tear it apart, like a cloud.

00:22:41.350 --> 00:22:44.440
Looking for, find it,

00:22:45.400 --> 00:22:49.280
So we can come closer together.

00:22:51.350 --> 00:22:55.810
I hear that the next episode is based on Sakaguchi Ango's 「Meiji-era Ango Detective Stories "Masked Mansion"」!

00:22:55.810 --> 00:22:57.270
Let's give it a read!

00:22:57.270 --> 00:23:01.980
Wow! Mitsuko, Fumihiko and Kigihiko are in the original, too!

00:23:01.980 --> 00:23:05.150
Also, Komamori, Inamori, Mizuhiko, Tsuchihiko...

00:23:05.150 --> 00:23:06.960
...how many relatives are there?!

00:23:07.530 --> 00:23:09.880
It says they have a disease that makes them collapse when they see someone's face,

00:23:09.880 --> 00:23:11.760
so they've been made to wear masks their entire lives.

00:23:11.760 --> 00:23:14.010
That's Sakaguchi Ango for you: so original!

00:23:14.010 --> 00:23:16.140
Wait, are we just going to leave it at that?!

00:23:16.140 --> 00:23:17.470
Next time on UN-GO:

00:23:17.470 --> 00:23:18.140
Masked Mansion!

00:23:18.380 --> 00:23:19.890
Who's Kazamori?!
